==Turkish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[jɯɫˈdɯʐ]|lang=tr}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|otk|tr}} ''yultuz'', from {{etyl|trk-pro|tr}} {{m|trk-pro|*jul-duŕ||star}}. Compare {{cog|az|ulduz}}; {{cog|ba|йондоҙ}}; {{cog|chg|sc=fa-Arab|یولدوز|tr=yulduz}}; {{cog|dlg|һулус|tr=hulus}}; {{cog|gag|yıldız}}; {{cog|krc|жулдуз|tr=culduz}}, {{m|krc|джулдуз|tr=culduz}}; {{cog|kaa|juldız}}; {{cog|kk|жұлдыз}}; {{cog|kjh|чылтыс}}; {{cog|kum|юлдуз|tr=yulduz}}; {{cog|ky|жылдыз}}; {{cog|nog|юлдыз}}; {{cog|cjs|чылтыс|tr=çıltıs}}; {{cog|alt|јылдыс|tr=cıldıs}}; {{cog|tt|yoldız}}; {{cog|tk|ýyldyz}}; {{cog|tyv|сылдыс}}; {{cog|ug|sc=ug-Arab|يۇلتۇز}}; {{cog|uz|yulduz}}; {{cog|sah|сулус}}, {{cog|cv|ҫӑлтӑр}}.

===Noun===
{{tr-noun|ı|lar}}

# {{label|tr|astronomy}} [[star]]
# A widely-known person; a [[celebrity]].
# [[actor|Actors]] in [[lead]]ing [[role]]s in [[movie]]s, television shows and other [[dramatic]] [[media]].
# An [[asterisk]] ([[*]]).
# A [[symbol]] used to rate [[quality]], notably used for [[hotels]], with ratings from 1 (poor quality) to 5 stars (top quality).

